<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constitutio Antoniniana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">212 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Edict of Caracalla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Constitutio Antoniniana, also called the Edict of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracalla">Caracalla</a>, was a decree issued by the Roman emperor Caracalla in 212 CE. It granted Roman citizenship to nearly all free inhabitants of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. It is often seen as a landmark in the integration of the empire's diverse populations, though it may also have aimed to increase tax revenue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constitutio-antoniniana.jpg" alt="Constitutio Antoniniana" width="253" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gie%C3%9Fen,_MS_Papyrus_Gissensis_40_Constitutio_Antoniniana_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
